&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;As an Accounting Intern, you&#39;ll join the Accounting team within Finance and get hands-on experience across a wide range of accounting operations. You&#39;ll collaborate with teams like Tax, FP&amp;amp;A, Treasury, and Source-to-Pay to support day-to-day processes, month/quarter-end close, and accounting transformation projects. You&#39;ll contribute real work from balance sheet reconciliations to system implementations, gaining exposure across multiple accounting functions and international stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare assigned balance sheet reconciliations, journal entries, and supporting schedules for month-end close cycles with guidance and review from Accounting team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Global GL Operations, Revenue Accounting, Digital Asset Inventory Accounting, and Capital Markets/Prime Financing Accounting, working with US and international stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to critical accounting projects such as new system logic implementations, process enhancements, or product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits by preparing documentation, including non-US subsidiary statutory financial statements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain process documentation and ensure adherence to internal controls, policies, and procedures throughout all assigned workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a BA/BS degree in Accounting or a related field with foundational knowledge of US GAAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated analytical ability applied to accounting or finance contexts, such as reconciliations, variance analysis, or financial modeling through coursework, projects, or prior experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple concurrent tasks and meet deadlines, including prioritizing across competing workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SQL, Snowflake, Looker, or similar analytics tools, or experience with digital assets and the crypto economy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position ID: P78074&lt;/p&gt;
