&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;As a Complaints Analyst on the Global Complaints team within Customer Experience, you&#39;ll investigate and resolve consumer, regulatory, and litigation support complaints to deliver fair outcomes for Coinbase customers. The Global Complaints team is responsible for handling complaints end-to-end across three units, and you&#39;ll own assigned cases from intake through resolution, ensuring every customer receives a thorough, accurate, and timely response. This role is fully onsite at Coinbase&#39;s Luxembourg office and requires working in the office five days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve assigned complaints by gathering account data, transaction history, and customer communications, delivering accurate responses within defined SLA timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain complete case records in Salesforce, including investigation notes, resolution rationale, and customer correspondence, and submit cases for QC review before closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex or ambiguous cases to your Supervisor or Complaints Lead with clear documentation of the issue and your initial assessment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag recurring complaint patterns or potential process gaps to leadership to support continuous improvement across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in calibration sessions, training, and nesting requirements to stay aligned on evolving quality standards and process updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2 years of experience in complaints handling, customer service, or dispute resolution within financial services, fintech, or a regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to draft clear, accurate written responses to customer complaints, with experience applying documented procedures and escalation paths in a structured environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of meeting SLA and quality targets in a high-volume, QC-reviewed production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in English (reading, writing, and speaking) with the ability to work defined shift patterns as required by the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional-level fluency in French (reading, writing, and speaking) with the ability to investigate and respond to complaints from French-speaking customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PID: P72333&lt;/p&gt;
