&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Learning Intern on the Coinbase Learning team within the People organization, you&#39;ll help design, deliver, and improve the programs that unlock growth for every Coinbase employee. You&#39;ll build AI-powered learning content, coordinate high-impact programs, and use data to drive measurable improvements across our learning portfolio, working at the intersection of instructional design and emerging AI capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and iterate learning content (presentations, guides, videos, Confluence pages) using AI tools to accelerate development cycles and improve content quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and produce instructor-led learning sessions and L&amp;amp;D offsites from scheduling through day-of execution, managing logistics and audience engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype AI-assisted learning experiences such as adaptive practice exercises, AI-generated scenario simulations, or on-demand skill-building resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze program evaluation and engagement data using AI-assisted methods to surface insights and recommend improvements to learning experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate program documentation and communication channels, ensuring employees can easily discover and access learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree or certificate in adult education, HR, organizational psychology, instructional design, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in Google Workspace (Slides, Sheets, Docs) with experience building polished slide decks and written materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in an administrative, coordination, or operations role where you managed multiple concurrent tasks with competing deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using generative AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude) to draft, edit, or design content, with the ability to articulate when AI output requires human judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
