&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Singapore Operations Manager reports to the Coinbase Singapore (CBSG) Country Director and plays a critical role in scaling our regulated business under MAS. This role owns the design and execution of operational frameworks across trading, staking, and custody — ensuring CBSG operates with the rigor, resilience, and regulatory alignment expected of a licensed capital markets dealer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Country Director in overseeing operational functions within CBSG and across intragroup and third-party providers, ensuring delivery aligns with MAS regulations and contractual obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain operational policies, procedures, SLA frameworks, and risk management processes across key business workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain supervision frameworks across CBSG&#39;s trading, staking, and custody operations in line with MAS regulatory and best-practice requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain robust operational resilience frameworks, including risk identification, contingency planning, and vulnerability mitigation to protect business continuity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate operational incident responses, facilitating timely communication with internal stakeholders, regulators, and third-party service providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams — including Legal, Compliance, Finance, Product, and Security — to project manage critical operations and risk-related initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support first-line-of-defense operations across launch assessments, approvals, staffing, and audit activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in Singapore financial services, capital markets, or operations strategy, including 5+ years in a supervisory capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a MAS-regulated capital markets dealer, with focus on trade supervision across crypto, equities, or derivatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience serving as senior management, director, or an appointed representative of a MAS-regulated entity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to develop and improve operational processes to drive efficiency at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills with proven ability to engage and influence senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills; able to produce externally ready materials with minimal review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P78202&lt;/p&gt;
