&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern on the Policy team, you&#39;ll get hands-on exposure to how Coinbase shapes crypto policy in Washington and beyond. Depending on where the team needs support, you may spend the summer on more outward-facing, community engagement work, or on more technical, research-driven policy analysis — sometimes a mix of both. The strongest candidates genuinely care about digital assets policy, work well with others, and can flex between hands-on advocacy work and detailed technical analysis depending on what the team needs that week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support a mix of policy workstreams, from advocacy, community engagement, and stakeholder outreach to technical research, regulatory analysis, and briefing materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft policy materials such as talking points, white papers, social media posts, presentation decks, and short and long-form articles for external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research on legislative, regulatory, and policy developments and synthesize findings into actionable briefs for the Policy team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational support on key deliverables including drafting, proofreading, data compilation, and project coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team player who can flex between grassroots/community-facing work and more technical, substantive research depending on team needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguity, able to make progress on undefined or evolving problems without needing every detail spelled out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree or certificate in public policy, political science, law, international relations, or a related field, with a genuine interest in US policy and government&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated research capability, including experience producing written analysis of legislative, regulatory, or policy topics (academic or professional)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, self-starter mindset with the ability to manage multiple concurrent deliverables with minimal supervision over a 12-week engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
