&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Real Estate &amp;amp; Builds Intern on the Employee &amp;amp; Workplace Experience team, you&#39;ll spend 12 weeks contributing to a project focused on standardizing and future-proofing our real estate strategy and workplace experience. You&#39;ll work closely with Design, Builds, and Workplace Experience teams - partnering with cross-functional stakeholders to improve processes and drive consistency across our portfolio. This role offers hands-on exposure to how projects move from inception to completion, giving you a front-row seat to the collaboration, decision-making, and execution that shape our workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a standardization initiative that establishes scalable frameworks for how we plan, design, and deliver workplace experiences across our portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Design, Builds, and Workplace Experience teams to identify opportunities to streamline processes and create consistency in project execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional project cycles from inception to completion - participating in planning, stakeholder alignment, milestone tracking, and post-project evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and synthesize industry trends, benchmarks, and internal data to inform recommendations that future-proof our real estate strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop tools, playbooks, templates, or guidelines that enable teams to execute standards more efficiently and with greater consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree or certificate in real estate, business, urban planning, facilities management, project management, or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to project management fundamentals, including planning, timeline tracking, and milestone reporting, with experience collaborating across multiple teams or stakeholders on shared deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to synthesize data, benchmarks, and qualitative input into clear, structured recommendations for cross-functional audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating documentation such as playbooks, process maps, or presentations through coursework, projects, or prior internships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in workplace strategy, employee experience, or real estate operations, demonstrated through coursework, projects, volunteer work, or self-directed learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
