&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As the Regional Security Manager, APAC, you&#39;ll lead the development and execution of Coinbase&#39;s regional security strategy on the Global Security team, protecting our people, workplaces, and operations across a diverse and rapidly evolving region. You&#39;ll own the physical security program for APAC offices, critical facilities, and data centers, partnering with business leaders and cross-functional teams to manage risk, strengthen resilience, and drive incident response across multiple countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the APAC physical security operating plan, regional risk register, site security standards, and remediation priorities across offices, critical facilities, and data centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead site assessments, vulnerability reviews, security hardening projects, new office openings, relocations, and security system deployments across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the regional escalation point and Incident Commander for significant security events, coordinating the GSOC, workplace teams, vendors, building management, and emergency services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern regional access control, badging, visitor management, secure area access, and audit readiness while managing contracted security providers through SLAs, KPIs, and QBRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain regional policies, SOPs, playbooks, drills, tabletop exercises, and employee-facing security guidance informed by APAC threat intelligence and local conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in physical security, risk, or resilience operations within a multinational organization, including 5+ years leading APAC regional security programs across multiple countries and sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience serving as Incident Commander during complex, cross-functional, or high-consequence security events with documented outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience implementing and managing access control, CCTV, alarm, visitor management, and guard force systems across multiple facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience conducting risk and vulnerability assessments and converting findings into measurable, time-bound remediation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record managing security vendors through SLAs, KPIs, QBRs, performance improvement plans, and contract renewals in APAC markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
