&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Coinbase Corporate Security (CorpSec) is seeking a Security Engineer to build and maintain security controls that protect corporate infrastructure, user devices, enterprise applications, and network communications. You&#39;ll partner closely with IT and engineering teams to identify risks and ship tailored solutions that keep users secure without introducing unnecessary friction, directly protecting Coinbase&#39;s most sensitive data and critical assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain security solutions to harden Coinbase&#39;s macOS, Chromebook, and mobile endpoints, focusing on secure configurations, compliance, threat detection, and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform security reviews on enterprise systems and software that enable user productivity across the corporate environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional partners to integrate endpoint and SaaS security into broader corporate engineering initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and close data exfiltration paths introduced by local AI agents and developer tooling (e.g., coding assistants, LLM harnesses) running on corporate endpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance and code review support to engineers on the CorpSec team, raising the security bar across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in security engineering, with at least 2 years securing macOS or similar user endpoints in an enterprise environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to write production code (services, integrations, automations) that supports corporate infrastructure security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scoping, prioritizing, and shipping security projects end-to-end with minimal direction in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with device trust, zero trust network access, or endpoint communication security products (e.g., Cloudflare, Prisma Access, Zscaler).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
