&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, Backend on the Client Lifecycle team within the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Institutional&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; group, you&#39;ll own the backend systems that take institutional clients from application to first trade and keep them operating independently once they&#39;re live. You&#39;ll design and scale Unified Business Onboarding, KYC Refresh, provisioning, and the access-control stack, partnering closely with Compliance, Identity, Onboarding Ops, and every Prime product team to ship onboarding and access controls for new products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own backend services that move institutional clients from application to first trade, including Unified Business Onboarding, KYC Refresh, and provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive onboarding automation, including automated screening, risk scoring, and auto-provisioning, so low-risk clients complete onboarding without an ops ticket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design and implementation of Organizations Service as the source of truth for institutional client data, including data quality, entity uniqueness, and Salesforce decoupling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Compliance, Onboarding Ops, Identity, and Prime product teams to ship onboarding and access controls for new products including FCM, Hudson derivatives, and Prime Custody.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the access-control stack (roles, permissions, policies, and consensus) so complex institutions can operate on Prime without opening a ticket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and raise the technical bar through design reviews, incident response, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of backend software engineering experience, including designing, building, and maintaining production services at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience with Go (or similar), gRPC/Protobuf, relational data stores, and observability tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of composing and scaling service-oriented architectures with demonstrated practice of writing well-tested, production-grade code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated, high-integrity domains such as identity, access control, KYC/AML, or financial onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
